Arg parser with the set of args from the shell script.

This drops the '--no<flag>' variant of each boolean arg, because they didn't seem to be used and would have been complex to add.

Usage: chromeos-install [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --dst <DST>
          Destination device

      --skip_dst_removable
          Skip check to ensure destination is not removable

  -y, --yes
          Answer yes to everything

      --skip_rootfs
          Skip installing the rootfs; Only set up partition table and clear and reinstall the stateful partition

      --preserve_stateful
          Don't create a new filesystem for the stateful partition. Be careful using this as this may make the stateful partition not mountable

      --payload_image <PAYLOAD_IMAGE>
          Path to a Chromium OS image to install onto the device's hard drive

      --pmbr_code <PMBR_CODE>
          Path to PMBR code to be installed

      --target_bios <TARGET_BIOS>
          Bios type to boot with (see postinst --bios)

      --debug
          Show debug output

      --storage_diags
          Print storage diagnostic information on failure

      --skip_gpt_creation
          Skips creating the GPT partition table

      --lab_preserve_logs <LAB_PRESERVE_LOGS>
          Path to a file containing logs to be preserved

      --skip_postinstall
          Skip postinstall for situations where you're building for a non-native arch. Note that this will probably break verity

      --minimal_copy
          Minimal copy of partitions

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
